Z||000000||Leadfoot||09-13-2001||08:00 PM||||Ok so on my way home from work my clutch just went limp.  After the car cooled down the clutch worked again.  Seems like the heat from the engine is causing the seals on the slave cylinder to leak but I don't see and oil.  Does someone know what might be happening here?||||reg||5
Z||000001||theogre||09-13-2001||08:28 PM||||flush new fluid thru it. That's a sign of fluid boil. Read my brake fluid article.<P>No, it's not common fo clutch to boil but if the fluid is wet it can happen. This is the first thing I'de check. It's cheap. the Valvoline fluid I like is only about $5 a quart.<P>Once you do the clutch, use the rest to do the brakes. (You likely need 2 quarts to do both.) <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 09-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||BlackDragon||09-13-2001||09:10 PM||||also check the slave cylinder, it could be bad, i had an rx-7 that did the same thing<P>------------------<BR>WTB:CHEAP black standard fiero. no engine is fine, any model/condition gray interior is a plus. must have title||||reg||1
Z||000003||qwikgta||09-13-2001||09:32 PM||||When this happened to me it was both my clutch master and slave cylinders that were bad, never saw any leak until it finally blew.<P>For what it is worth, after i replaced them and bleed the system, it has worked great, should have done it months ago.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://www.homestead.com/robsfieroproject   <BR>http://www.vafieros.com<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigpic2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
